cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or research artifact, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "CoDA Authorization: Bounded Chain-of-Delegation Authorization for Cross-Domain Industrial Digital Twin Agents"

type: software
version: 0.1.0

authors:
  - family-names: "Manasrah"
    given-names: "Ahmed"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Amanasrah78/CoDA-Authorization"

abstract: >-
  CoDA is a bounded Chain-of-Delegation authorization framework for
  cross-domain Industrial Digital Twin agents. This repository provides a
  reconstructed reference implementation of the CoDA authorization model,
  including delegation-credential validation, Ed25519 signature verification,
  bounded delegation depth, monotonic scope reduction, contextual and usage
  constraints, revocation, short-lived JWT capabilities, Open Policy Agent
  integration, post-authorization commitment anchoring, functional tests,
  and reproducible performance benchmarks.

keywords:
  - authorization
  - delegation
  - chain of delegation
  - industrial digital twin
  - agentic AI
  - decentralized identity
  - capability-based access control
  - Open Policy Agent
  - zero trust

